# What the image is built from (Dockerfile), as an allowlist: everything is left out, then the project's
# manifest and lockfile, its YAML and generated pages, and its folders are let back in, and, within
# those, what is never the image's is left out again: dotfiles (the settings file and keys, an editor's
# or an assistant's local settings), env files under any name, keys and certificates, logs, and what a
# server writes where it runs. A file only your own global gitignore hides still never reaches the image.
